Q: Right way to throw errors using $PSCmdlet.ThrowTerminatingError() A: <p>Even the question you ask might result in <strong>opinion-based</strong> answers, I understand why you question this also knowing that <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/powershell/scripting/learn/deep-dives/everything-about-exceptions#pscmdletthrowterminatingerror" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>$PSCmdlet.ThrowTerminatingError()</code></a> points to the invocation rather than into your own script as <code>throw</code> and <code>Write-Error</code> do. Saying that, you do lay the responsibility at the caller and therefore it isn't a bad idea to supply it with additional information as <code>errorId</code>, <code>errorCategory</code> and <code>targetObject</code>. That way the caller might also has the opportunity to action on the problem <em>programmatically</em> (assuming that the caller isn't a LLM where a &quot;<em>simple string</em>&quot; might be sufficient😀).<br />
Anyways, to be honest, I have had the same requirement and up till now have been using a function to simplify this but the difficulty there is that you create a new scope which isn't the case with the <code>catch</code> you purpose yourself which on the otherhand, is quiet verbose (compared to <code>throw</code> and <code>Write-Error</code>).<br />
But there is a also a <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/powershell/module/microsoft.powershell.core/about/about_trap" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>Trap</code></a> keyword, which is quite similar but only needs to be setup once. You might even consider to only <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/powershell/module/microsoft.powershell.core/about/about_trap?#trapping-specific-errors" rel="nofollow noreferrer">trap specific errors</a> for example an <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/api/system.argumentexception" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>ArgumentException</code></a> (which is most likely the case given where you ask for).<br />
Or create a custom exception so that you can still <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/powershell/scripting/learn/deep-dives/everything-about-exceptions#re-throwing-an-exception" rel="nofollow noreferrer">re-throw</a> <em>any</em> other unexpected exception:</p>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>class CallerError : Exception {
    CallerError($Message) : base($Message) { }
}

function a {
    [CmdletBinding()]param()
    Trap [CallerError] {
        $PSCmdlet.ThrowTerminatingError($_)
    }
    Throw [CallerError]'In your dreams'
}

function b { a }

b
</code></pre>
